window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2d8d28cbaa954fc4"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security-cloud-faq\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security-cloud\">Codex Security Cloud 常见问题</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>以下解答适用于 Codex Security Cloud。有关安装和首次扫描，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">云端设置</a>。本地扫描请参阅单独的 <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">plugin</a> 和 <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI</a> 指南。</p> <p><a id=\"billing\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">计费</h2> <p><a id=\"how-are-cloud-scans-billed\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cloud\">Cloud 扫描如何计费？</h3> <p>在 2026 年 10 月 1 日太平洋时间中午 12:53 之后设置的代码库扫描和持续扫描，将根据令牌使用量按你的方案费率计费；具体以 credits 或美元计价，取决于你的账单方案。对于<a href=\"#/article/a-2d8d28cbaa954fc4?anchor=do-i-get-a-free-scanning-period-or-free-scanning-credits\">符合资格的账户</a>，系统会先使用免费扫描额度，之后才对付费使用量计费。</p> <p>这部分用量不包含在你的方案所含用量额度内。</p> <p>在该截止时间之前设置的持续扫描，可以免费使用至 2026 年 10 月 21 日。此后，如果你启用了付费使用量，就会根据账户账单方案按常规令牌费率计费；否则扫描会暂停。</p> <h3 id=\"do-i-get-a-free-scanning-period-or-free-scanning-credits\">是否有免费扫描期或免费扫描额度？</h3> <p>你获得的优惠取决于账户是否在 2026 年 10 月 1 日太平洋时间中午 12:53 之前设置了持续扫描：</p> <ul> <li>如果已设置，符合条件的持续扫描可免费使用至 2026 年 10 月 21 日。免费期不适用于代码库扫描，也不适用于在 2026 年 10 月 1 日太平洋时间中午 12:53 之后设置的持续扫描。</li> <li>如果没有设置，符合条件的账户会获得 500 美元的免费扫描额度，而不是免费持续扫描期。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"how-do-free-scanning-credits-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">免费扫描额度如何使用？</h3> <p>代码库扫描和持续扫描共用同一笔免费额度。在同一工作区中，所有人共享这笔额度。免费扫描额度不会过期。</p> <p>免费额度用完后，后续扫描将按照你个人账户或工作区的账单方案计费。</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-when-the-free-continuous-scanning-period-ends\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">免费持续扫描期结束后会怎样？</h3> <p>选择 <strong>Keep scans running（继续运行扫描）</strong>并启用付费使用量，即可在免费期结束后继续运行这些扫描。之后会按照你个人账户或工作区账单方案的常规令牌费率计费。</p> <p>如果你选择退出，或未启用付费使用量，这些扫描会在免费期结束时暂停。之后可以选择 <strong>Re-enable scans（重新启用扫描）</strong>并启用付费使用量。如果你在工作区中没有相应权限，请联系工作区所有者代为选择。</p> <p><a id=\"where-can-i-see-token-usage-and-charges\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">在哪里查看令牌用量和费用？</h3> <p>在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中打开某次扫描，即可查看该次扫描使用的令牌和费用。将鼠标悬停在令牌数量上，可以查看输入令牌、缓存输入令牌和输出令牌。缓存输入令牌已包含在输入令牌数量中，不会额外叠加。</p> <p>用量页面显示的是扣除免费扫描额度或账单豁免之前的费用，并会同时显示免费扫描额度所覆盖的金额。</p> <p>标记为“Exempt from billing. No charges apply.”（免于计费，不产生费用）的扫描不会产生费用，即使页面显示了令牌用量和成本也是如此。</p> <p><a id=\"scanning\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">扫描</h2> <p><a id=\"does-the-project-need-to-be-built-for-scanning\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">扫描前是否必须构建项目？</h3> <p>Codex Security 无需等到项目成功构建，就可以分析源代码。验证问题时，可能需要依赖项或可正常工作的构建环境，以便重现问题。请在 <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex 云环境</a>中配置这些要求。</p> <p>如果验证无法运行，请检查该发现通过源代码能够证明什么，以及哪些结论仍取决于运行时或部署行为。</p> <p><a id=\"what-languages-are-supported\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">支持哪些编程语言？</h3> <p>Codex Security 可以分析多种语言的源代码。结果取决于模型对该语言和框架的推理能力，以及可用的代码库上下文。扫描成功并不代表各种语言或组件都具有相同的覆盖范围。请查看报告，确认实际审核了哪些范围。</p> <p><a id=\"how-do-repository-scans-and-commit-monitoring-differ\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">代码库扫描和提交监控有什么区别？</h3> <p><strong>One-Time Scan（单次扫描）</strong>只审核一次代码库。<strong>Continuous Scanning（持续扫描）</strong>会监控新的提交，也可以审核选定的提交历史。首次扫描后，请通过<a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8?anchor=5-monitor-new-commits\">监控新的提交</a>启用此功能。</p> <p><a id=\"can-i-pause-commit-monitoring\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">可以暂停提交监控吗？</h3> <p>打开 <strong>Repositories（代码库）</strong>，选择相应代码库，再打开 <strong>Monitoring settings（监控设置）</strong>。将监控设为 <strong>Paused（已暂停）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Save（保存）</strong>。你可以在相同设置中重新启用监控。</p> <p><a id=\"can-i-edit-the-threat-model\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">可以编辑威胁模型吗？</h3> <p>可以。若架构、部署方式或安全假设发生变化，请在受监控代码库的 <strong>Monitoring settings（监控设置）</strong>中更新威胁模型。<a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">威胁模型指南</a>说明了应包含哪些内容。更改会应用于未来的扫描。</p> <p><a id=\"findings-and-validation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">发现项与验证</h2> <p><a id=\"what-does-validation-establish\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">验证能够证明什么？</h3> <p>请阅读附在具体发现项上的证据。源代码分析可以证明存在一条有漏洞的代码路径；执行证据则可以表明某个特定的复现程序或测试实际展示了该问题。</p> <p>发现项记录的状态和严重性有助于整理审核工作。请根据底层证据和前置条件，判断该问题是否适用于你的系统，以及需要修复什么。</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-if-validation-fails\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">如果验证失败，会发生什么？</h3> <p>检查尝试过的验证方式和任何可用日志。复现程序失败可能表示该问题不适用，但也可能是因为环境或测试不合适。排除指出的缺口之前，不要驳回该发现，也不要声称问题已成功复现。</p> <p><a id=\"what-if-the-scan-reports-no-findings\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">如果扫描没有报告任何发现项呢？</h3> <p>确认扫描已经完成，并且审核了预期的代码库和修订版本。阅读记录在案的限制或未完成工作。即使扫描没有报告发现，也仍有可能漏掉漏洞。</p> <p><a id=\"fixes\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">修复</h2> <p><a id=\"does-codex-security-apply-patches-automatically\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-security\">Codex Security 会自动应用补丁吗？</h3> <p>具体操作取决于发现项的类型。对于代码库中的发现，选择 <strong>Fix with Codex（使用 Codex 修复）</strong>会开始一个对话，请 Codex 验证问题、实施修复并运行相关测试。请在该对话中审核更改。</p> <p>如果某个发现项提供了建议补丁，请在选择 <strong>Create draft pull request（创建草稿 pull request）</strong>之前审核差异。创建草稿并不代表修复已经合并。</p> <p><a id=\"how-do-i-know-whether-a-patch-fixed-the-issue\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">如何确认补丁是否修复了问题？</h3> <p>审核补丁的验证证据，包括原始问题是否仍能复现，以及正常行为是否仍然有效。如果验证尚未完成，请在该发现项中保留这项不确定性。仅有建议补丁、草稿 pull request 或状态更改，都不能证明修复已经生效。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security-cloud-faq\">Codex Security Cloud FAQ</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>These answers apply to Codex Security Cloud. For installation and a first scan, use <a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Cloud setup</a>. Local scans have separate <a href=\"#/article/a-bec1e26cb654a758\">plugin</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-1716f9f1a07bca7e\">CLI</a> guides.</p> <h2 id=\"billing\">Billing</h2> <h3 id=\"how-are-cloud-scans-billed\">How are Cloud scans billed?</h3> <p>Repository scans and continuous scans set up after October 1, 2026, at 12:53 PM Pacific are billed based on token usage at your plan's rates, in credits or USD depending on your billing plan. For <a href=\"#/article/a-2d8d28cbaa954fc4?anchor=do-i-get-a-free-scanning-period-or-free-scanning-credits\">eligible accounts</a>, free scanning credits apply before paid usage is billed.</p> <p>This usage is not covered by your plan's included usage allowance.</p> <p>Continuous scans set up before that cutoff are free until October 21, 2026. After that, they are billed at regular token rates under your account's billing plan if you enable paid usage. Otherwise, they pause.</p> <h3 id=\"do-i-get-a-free-scanning-period-or-free-scanning-credits\">Do I get a free scanning period or free scanning credits?</h3> <p>What you receive depends on whether your account had continuous scanning set up before October 1, 2026, at 12:53 PM Pacific:</p> <ul> <li>If it did, your covered continuous scans remain free until October 21, 2026. This free period doesn't cover repository scans or continuous scanning set up after October 1, 2026, at 12:53 PM Pacific.</li> <li>If it didn't, eligible accounts receive $500 in free scanning credits instead of the free continuous-scanning period.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"how-do-free-scanning-credits-work\">How do free scanning credits work?</h3> <p>Repository scans and continuous scanning use the same free balance. In a workspace, everyone shares that balance. These free scanning credits don't expire.</p> <p>When the free balance runs out, further scanning is billed under your account's or workspace's billing plan.</p> <h3 id=\"what-happens-when-the-free-continuous-scanning-period-ends\">What happens when the free continuous-scanning period ends?</h3> <p>Select <strong>Keep scans running</strong> and enable paid usage to continue these scans after the free period. They are then billed at regular token rates under your account's or workspace's billing plan.</p> <p>If you opt out or don't enable paid usage, those scans pause when the free period ends. Select <strong>Re-enable scans</strong> to enable paid usage afterward. In a workspace, ask a workspace owner to make this choice if you don't have permission.</p> <h3 id=\"where-can-i-see-token-usage-and-charges\">Where can I see token usage and charges?</h3> <p>Open a scan in <strong>Scans</strong> to review its token usage and cost. Hover over the token count to see input, cached input, and output tokens. Cached input is included in the input count, not added on top of it.</p> <p>Usage shows the cost before free scanning credits or billing exemptions, along with any amount covered by free scanning credits.</p> <p>Scans marked \"Exempt from billing. No charges apply.\" incur no charges, even when they show token usage and cost.</p> <h2 id=\"scanning\">Scanning</h2> <h3 id=\"does-the-project-need-to-be-built-for-scanning\">Does the project need to be built for scanning?</h3> <p>Codex Security can analyze source without a successful build. Validation may need dependencies or a working build to reproduce an issue. Configure those requirements in the <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex cloud environment</a>.</p> <p>If validation can't run, inspect what the finding establishes from source and what still depends on runtime or deployment behavior.</p> <h3 id=\"what-languages-are-supported\">What languages are supported?</h3> <p>Codex Security analyzes source across languages. Results depend on the model's ability to reason about the language and framework, and on the available repository context. A successful scan doesn't imply equal coverage across languages or components. Check the report for the scope actually reviewed.</p> <h3 id=\"how-do-repository-scans-and-commit-monitoring-differ\">How do repository scans and commit monitoring differ?</h3> <p>A <strong>One-Time Scan</strong> reviews the repository once. <strong>Continuous Scanning</strong> monitors new commits and can review selected commit history. Enable it after the first scan using <a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8?anchor=5-monitor-new-commits\">Monitor new commits</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"can-i-pause-commit-monitoring\">Can I pause commit monitoring?</h3> <p>Open <strong>Repositories</strong>, select the repository, and open <strong>Monitoring settings</strong>. Set monitoring to <strong>Paused</strong> and select <strong>Save</strong>. You can enable it again from the same settings.</p> <h3 id=\"can-i-edit-the-threat-model\">Can I edit the threat model?</h3> <p>Yes. Update it in the monitored repository's <strong>Monitoring settings</strong> when the architecture, deployment, or security assumptions change. The <a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">threat-model guide</a> explains what to include. Changes apply to future scans.</p> <h2 id=\"findings-and-validation\">Findings and validation</h2> <h3 id=\"what-does-validation-establish\">What does validation establish?</h3> <p>Read the evidence attached to the particular finding. Source analysis can establish a vulnerable code path. Execution evidence can show that a specific reproducer or test demonstrated the issue.</p> <p>A finding's recorded status and severity help organize review. Use the underlying evidence and prerequisites to decide whether it applies to your system and what to fix.</p> <h3 id=\"what-happens-if-validation-fails\">What happens if validation fails?</h3> <p>Inspect the attempted validation and any available logs. A failed reproducer can mean the issue doesn't apply, but it can also mean the environment or test was unsuitable. Resolve the stated gap before dismissing the finding or claiming that it was reproduced.</p> <h3 id=\"what-if-the-scan-reports-no-findings\">What if the scan reports no findings?</h3> <p>Confirm that the scan completed and reviewed the intended repository and revision. Read any recorded limits or unfinished work. A scan that reports no findings can still miss vulnerabilities.</p> <h2 id=\"fixes\">Fixes</h2> <h3 id=\"does-codex-security-apply-patches-automatically\">Does Codex Security apply patches automatically?</h3> <p>The action depends on the finding. <strong>Fix with Codex</strong> on a repository finding starts a conversation that asks Codex to verify the issue, implement a fix, and run relevant tests. Review the changes in that conversation.</p> <p>For a finding with a suggested patch, review the diff before selecting <strong>Create draft pull request</strong>. Creating the draft doesn't merge the fix.</p> <h3 id=\"how-do-i-know-whether-a-patch-fixed-the-issue\">How do I know whether a patch fixed the issue?</h3> <p>Review the patch's validation evidence, including whether the original issue still reproduces and whether legitimate behavior still works. If validation wasn't completed, keep that uncertainty with the finding. A proposed patch, draft pull request, or status change alone doesn't verify a fix.</p>"};
